{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/kernel/kernel.go at exact 4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87 on request/one-verified-world, under promise git:sha1…a6ffa61 on request git:sha1…35d8011\n\nImplements request 555f239cfad9d38d46016fb118161539235d8011 (verify the log once per signing command) at head 4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87, branch request/one-verified-world.\n\nWhat changed. A signing command used to read and verify the whole log three to six times. It now reads it once, and every later check reuses that one verified read.\n\n1. Measurements. These are on a frozen copy of artroom, comparing main 69018ecd with this head. Each figure is the median of three interleaved runs. Commands that append went from 26-46 s to 8-9 s and make no cold scan:\n- artifact, local: 38.0 s -\u003e 8.7 s\n- review-request, local: 38.1 s -\u003e 8.6 s\n- state accepted, local: 25.9 s -\u003e 8.6 s\n- state accepted, resident: 34.4 s -\u003e 8.4 s\n- ratify succeeds, local: 12.1 s -\u003e 8.3 s\nRefused ratify is unchanged at 7.7-7.9 s. Peak memory on the local route went from 1.1 GB to about 640 MB.\n\n2. One read. With a valid checkpoint, each single-act signing command makes exactly one complete verified read. TestSigningCommandsVerifyTheLogOnce counts the reads.\nTwo limits are recorded on the architecture page:\n- A chain of two or more acts makes one more read, for its scratch fold. The checkpoint material lacks the signed intent (actor, rests_on, schema), and the fold has no copy operation.\n- In a long-lived process, a seeded submitter makes one full read each time a checkpoint falls due.\n\n3. Replay lookups. Retry lookups and replay checks come from the session reader's verified dedup index, and only while that reader stands at exactly the current head.\n- The key is the kernel's key: target, actor key, namespace and key.\n- A conflicting act under a held key is still refused.\n- Each matched payload is read again by the tree its signature names, and every object is checked against its hash.\n\n4. Admission. Admission reuses a fold only where both the session fold and the session reader stand at exactly the head it judges. Otherwise it uses a private reader. The private reader consumes a signed checkpoint but writes nothing: no checkpoint, no ref or pointer repair, and no change to the witness. Nothing is reused from:\n- a resident's answer;\n- a caller's projection;\n- an audit that failed;\n- a fold that the rollback witness held back.\n\n5. Checkpoint cadence. A process that appends publishes exactly one checkpoint per interval, as main does.\n- Reading back the process's own appends (Reader.CatchUp) verifies the delta but publishes nothing.\n- A seeded submitter collects no checkpoint material. When a checkpoint falls due, it rebuilds by making one full read, and it publishes at that position.\n- TestAnAppendingProcessKeepsTheCheckpointCadence asserts the exact moves for both a resident and a signer. It is red at both earlier repair heads.\n\n6. Tests break each guard. Each guard was broken in a copy: 35 mutants, all red except M8. M8 survives only because an independent second guard blocks the same reuse; with both removed (M8b) it goes red. A checkpoint signed by another key is refused on the signing path. Two fresh adversarial reviews ran, at f24c12c7 and at fa478a38, and their findings are fixed here.\n\n7. Projections unchanged. After four kinds of accepted act on the frozen copy (artifact, review-request, state, ratify), the projection is byte-identical to a cold fold at the same head.\n\n8. Suite. go test -p 1 -count=1 -timeout 40m ./... passes at 4d5d9c2d (36 packages).\n\nArchitecture. The contracts of the kernel and app layers change as documented in docs/reference/architecture.md, layers 2, 4 and 5. There is no new format, persisted state or package.\nLock order: the sequencer lock, then snapshotMu (only tried, never waited for), then Reader.mu. The admission lock is never held together with snapshotMu.\n\nSecurity. Trust is unchanged. Only this process's own verified reads are reused, and only at a head its reader verified. Every actor signature is still verified on load, and the checkpoint carries event material only.\n\nSimplification. There is no new framework, and a redundant marker error is removed. On parent c4c2be71ea1a449f8f4819aa2897a2f26d501fcc: one verified load per command meets condition 2, per planner assert 637f7ac660a019cce750bc61080077fee2a678f7. A signing command still takes about one cold-fold time (about 8-9 s at artroom depth). That is not \"much less than a cold fold\", and step 2 (request d1b3d1b1d8a481ad0bda38d7b137764e0a3a28d3) is where that remains.","body":{"commit":"4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87","path":"internal/kernel/kernel.go"}}